,title,link,text,language,family
0,Nilotic peoples - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nilotic_peoples,"1 week ago - The Highland Nilotes are subdivided into two groups, the Kalenjin and the Datog. Kalenjin: Elgeyo, Kipsigis, Marakwet, Nandi, Pokot, Sabaot, Lembus, Terik and Tugen [Keiyo]",Nandi,Nilo-Saharan
1,Nilo-Saharan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nilo-Saharan_languages,"2 weeks ago - The Nilo-Saharan languages are a proposed linguistic family consisting of around 210 Native African languages spoken by somewhere around 70 million speakers, mainly in the upper parts of the Chari and Nile rivers, including historic Nubia, north of where the two tributaries of the Nile meet.",Nandi,Nilo-Saharan
2,Nandi people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nandi_people,"1 week ago - They speak the Nandi dialect, which is closely related to Kipsigis, a Kalenjin language part of the broader Nilo-Saharan linguistic family. With a population of nearly 1 million, they historically occupied the highland areas of the former Rift Valley Province of Kenya, in what is today Nandi County.",Nandi,Nilo-Saharan
3,Nandi | Spotify,https://open.spotify.com/artist/0G7X5hfVRnwfuuErO29lyy,"It also garnered many other nods including the South African Music Awards 2016 nomination for the Record of The Year category. In 2019, KO and Nandi released a follow up song to “Skhanda Love” titled “Say U Will”. The song has received major airplay on South African radio stations, it also reached number 1 on the music charts in its third week of release.",Nandi,Nilo-Saharan
4,The Nilotic people of Africa - i EXPLORE AFRICA,https://www.iexploreafrica.com/the-nilotic-people-of-africa/,"August 16, 2022 - Music and dance in almost all the Nilotes is a rite of passage handed down from generation to another. For instance, the high jump dance is a traditionally practiced among the Maasai, Samburu and Karamojong.",Nandi,Nilo-Saharan
